# Design and aesthetic constraints

## Typography and hierarchy

- Avoid flat, evenly-weighted type scales. Enforce high contrast between headings and body text.
- Use distinct font weights (e.g., pairing `font-medium` or `font-semibold` headers with regular body text).
- Never let type color default to pure harsh black (`#000000`) on pure white; use muted slate or zinc tokens (e.g., `text-zinc-900` or `text-slate-800`).

## Spacing and layout rhythm

- Avoid evenly distributed, overly spaced card layouts where every element has the exact same padding.
- Use tight, intentional groupings. Information density should vary depending on the component context.
- Rely on precise layout constraints (referencing concrete design systems like shadcn/ui or Radix primitives) rather than letting the model guess "modern padding".

## Color tokens and saturation

- Strictly ban overly saturated, glowing AI gradients (e.g., bright neon purple-to-blue default buttons).
- Limit primary accent colors to a single intentional hue. Neutral backgrounds must use subtle surface shifts (e.g., `bg-zinc-50` over `bg-white`) rather than stark white blocks.
- Borders must be extremely subtle (`border-zinc-200` or lighter), never heavy or high-contrast grey lines.

## Execution workflow

- Follow the confirmed UI plan and DESIGN.md. Inspect desktop and mobile together; batch corrections rather than repeatedly polishing.

## Project locks

- Analysis Desk: cool off-white surfaces, graphite text, cobalt actions and selection. Use the tokens in global.css.
- Public Sans is the only typeface. Light theme only.
- Use a text wordmark. Do not generate logos. Duck personality belongs in selected copy: “Get your ducks in a row,” “Pick your punt,” and occasional quack loading copy.
- Body, actions, and form labels are at least 1rem. Secondary metadata may use 0.875rem. Important chart labels must remain legible.
- Use rem for type and spacing; use px for border widths and radii. Main radius is 8px. Avoid pills.
- No uppercase kickers, colored eyebrows, gradients, or ornamental charts.
- Use semantic tokens instead of one-off component colors. Positive/negative colors encode actual category strength, never brand decoration.
- Use the statistics table on mobile and desktop, with horizontal scrolling contained inside the table. Mobile presentation controls live in the Board view sheet.
- Detailed weight editing opens on demand. Quiz category charts stay visible, above walkthrough answers and expanded in the Closest build panel.
- Use the existing Lucide React icons for action buttons; keep visible text labels.
- Local imports use @/. Cross-package imports use @draft-duck/core.
